**Verification of collinearity**: A→N = (√2/6)(−1715, 4165), A→P = √2(1400, −3400). Ratio: 1400/(−1715/6) = −240/49 and −3400/(4165/6) = −240/49. ✓

## Computing the Orthocenter H of △MOP

Factor out √2 and work in scaled coordinates (dividing by √2):
- M' = (2660, 1680), O' = (40320/17, 16800/17), P' = (3360, −3400)

**Altitude from M'** (⊥ to O'P'): Direction O'P' = (16800/17, −74600/17) ∝ (84, −373), so altitude direction = (373, 84).
